title: Build adversarial memory-model soundness fuzzer
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-04T05:31:38'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T07:51:17'
result: 'Added tests/ownership_fuzz.rs: proptest generator (200 cases) emitting random
  well-formed-ish ownership-stressing Jinn programs covering nested take, field/heap
  moves under if, container-read aliasing (v.get), copy of heap values, and rebind-after-move.
  Each program must either be cleanly rejected or run to completion with no abort
  (134)/segfault (139)/compiler ICE. Under the ci/sanitize.sh ASan+UBSan sweep the
  same corpus catches UAF/double-free/OOB in the Perceus + escape + tombstone passes.'
description: 'Adversarial memory-model soundness fuzzer (review P0-11 second half
  + 11_codegen_runtime). Current state: fuzz/ has lexer/parser/typer cargo-fuzz targets
  (front-end only); no end-to-end soundness fuzzing; no sanitizer CI (ci/sanitize.sh
  absent). Deliverable: (1) program-generator fuzzer emitting well-typed Jinn programs
  stressing Perceus (aliasing, take/borrow mixes, drop ordering, reuse pairs, vec/map
  churn, closures capturing refcounted values, actor channel handoff) and asserting:
  exit 0, no leaks (ASan), refcount invariants; (2) ci/sanitize.sh building runtime
  with -fsanitize=address,undefined and thread, running the conformance suites. Definition
  of done: fuzz target in fuzz/Cargo.toml runs 30 min clean (Phase A exit criterion);
  sanitize script wired into CI.'
